multivocal.m:
a. Signifying many different things; of manifold meaning;
   equivocal.
n. A multivocal word.

contexture.m:
n. The arrangement and union of the constituent parts of a
   thing; a weaving together of parts; structural character of a thing;
   system; constitution; texture.

strath.m:
n. A valley of considerable size, through which a river runs;
   a valley bottom; -- often used in composition with the name of the
   river; as, Strath Spey, Strathdon, Strathmore.

forfeiture.m:
n something that is lost or surrendered as a penalty; 
n a penalty for a fault or mistake that involves losing or giving up something
n the act of losing or surrendering something as a penalty for a mistake or fault or failure to perform etc.

amid.m:
prep. See Amidst.
prep. In the midst or middle of; surrounded or encompassed by;
   among.

disperse.m:
v. to cause to separate and go in different directions
v. move away from each other; 
v. separate (light) into spectral rays

attractive.m:
a. pleasing to the eye or mind especially through beauty or charm
s. having power to arouse interest
a. having the properties of a magnet; the ability to draw or pull;

poly-.m:
a. A combining form or prefix from Gr. poly`s, many; as,
   polygon, a figure of many angles; polyatomic, having many atoms;
   polychord, polyconic.

radio-.m:
A combining form indicating connection with, or relation to,
  a radius or ray; specifically (Anat.), with the radius of the forearm;
  as, radio-ulnar, radio-muscular, radio-carpal.
